# Runbooks

Runbooks contain reviewed, repeatable operational procedures. `docs/OPERATIONS.md` remains the current operations authority and links applicable runbooks.

Use `_template.md`. Every runbook states trigger and scope, prerequisites and authorization, exact project-owned commands, expected observations, stop conditions, rollback or recovery, retained evidence, and escalation. Keep unknown environment-specific details Open rather than inventing them.

## Guided procedure candidates

{{PROCEDURE_EVIDENCE}}

A procedure becomes eligible for a project-owned Skill only when its structured record is complete and Confirmed. Completeness requires Confirmed owner, trigger and scope, prerequisites and authorization, exact steps, expected observations or evidence, stop conditions, rollback or recovery, and escalation. Only complete Confirmed structured procedure records can produce an instruction-only `.claude/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md` through resumed `reporivet setup`. Do not pre-generate a project-specific Skill: no procedure is inferred or executed, and existing differing, stale, or arbitrary Skills are preserved rather than deleted. Keep Skill frontmatter instruction-only and least privilege, without settings grants, hooks, tools, shell, executor, or other runtime metadata.
